q:
An Nginx reverse proxy fronts a Node backend that streams a generative AI completion to the browser as Server-Sent Events. Run locally the tokens appear one by one; through Nginx the client receives nothing until the model has finished, and then the whole response arrives at once. The location block is:

location /api/chat/ {
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8080;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Connection "";
}

Which addition fixes the delivery?
